cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "ko-finance-asr-corrections: Frequency-annotated Korean ASR confusion pairs from finance/stock YouTube"
abstract: >-
  A frequency-annotated dictionary of Korean ASR misrecognition→correction pairs mined from
  auto-captions of Korean finance/stock YouTube, together with a standard-library benchmark
  that scores fixes and over-corrections together. Every pair carries an observed corpus
  frequency and verification provenance (two independent LLM auditors, an external registry
  check, and a promotion tier). Stock names, finance terms and number damage only — no person
  names and no source sentences. The data is a filtered snapshot of the production correction
  dictionary of the 껄무새 (Ggulmuse) pipeline.
authors:
  # Mononym/handle: CFF encodes a single-part personal name in `given-names`.
  - given-names: woongstardev
    alias: woongstardev
    website: "https://ggulmuse.woongstar.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/woongstardev/ko-finance-asr-corrections"
url: "https://ggulmuse.woongstar.com"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.0-dev
date-released: "2026-08-12"
# On the first public release, add the Zenodo concept DOI here so the citation is resolvable:
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
#       description: "Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest snapshot"
keywords:
  - Korean
  - ASR
  - speech recognition
  - error correction
  - confusion pairs
  - finance
  - post-processing
